  "$comment": [
    "Published RFC 8785 (JCS) canonicalization test vectors for AiGovOps Beacon.",
    "",
    "Beacon signs the CANONICAL BYTES of a receipt, so every implementation that",
    "signs or verifies must agree on those bytes exactly. Beacon has more than one",
    "canonicalizer and cannot collapse to a single file: server/src/lib/canonical.js",
    "is the reference; beacons/_common.py is the Python producer; and",
    "src/beacon_verify.py carries its own copy ON PURPOSE, because it is shipped",
    "into every audit bundle as one self-contained file an auditor can read in full.",
    "",
    "So agreement is MEASURED here instead of assumed. Each `canonical` value was",
    "produced by the JS reference and is asserted byte-for-byte by every other",
    "implementation's test suite. A new implementation in any language is expected",
    "to pass this file before it signs anything.",
    "",
    "Consumers:",
    "  tests/unit/test_canonicalization_vectors.py   (beacons/_common.py, src/beacon_verify.py)",
    "  server/test/unit/canonical-vectors.test.js    (server/src/lib/canonical.js, lab-service/shared/canonical.js)",
    "",
    "Regenerate ONLY if the canonical form itself changes, which is a signing-format",
    "change and needs a schema_version bump: any edit here invalidates existing",
    "signatures."
  ],
